course: dictionary
lesson: 9213
title: Solitary: alone and single
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Solitary means alone, with no one else around. A solitary animal lives on its own. Read the context: «Most kinds of bee live alone; a solitary bee lays its eggs in a hole in a wall, a hollow stem or a tunnel in the ground.» The words live alone tell you what solitary means.
explain: Solitary can also mean single, only one: «a solitary tree» is the only tree in the field. Ask: what word would fit here? Try alone or only one in the sentence instead of the hard word, and check that it still makes sense.
explain: A solitary place is lonely and far from people. Authors use this word to make you feel how far away everyone else is, so a solitary figure on a hill looks small and lonely.
fact: Solitary means alone, with no one else.
fact: A solitary animal lives on its own, while a social animal, like an ant or a wolf, lives in a group.
fact: «Solitary» can also mean single, as in «a solitary tree».
fact: Most kinds of bee live alone, and most solitary bees rarely sting.
fact: Real orangutans are quiet, mostly solitary apes that live only on the islands of Borneo and Sumatra, not kings of a monkey gang as in The Jungle Book.
exercise: «A solitary bee lays its eggs in a hole in a wall.» What does solitary mean here? | Working in a team with the other bees | *Living alone, with no other bees helping | Flying very fast | Stinging anyone who comes near
exercise: «The farmer stood by a solitary tree in the field.» What does solitary tell you about the tree? | *A tree that is the only one there | A tree that has been cut down | A tree with many friends nearby | A tree full of birds
exercise: Which animal is solitary? | *Tigers, which mostly live alone | Monkeys, which play in big troops | Wolves, which live in packs | Ants, which work together in a colony
test: «The orangutan is a quiet, mostly solitary ape.» What does solitary mean in this sentence? | Friendly and noisy | Hungry all day | *Mostly living on its own | Very fast and strong
test: Which sentence uses solitary to mean lonely and far from people? | The bus was full of cheerful passengers. | *The hut stood in a solitary place, far from any town. | The class sang together in the hall. | Every shop on the high street was open.
exam: Jayden reads, «King Louie rules a ruined temple, but real orangutans are quiet, mostly solitary apes.» What does solitary most likely mean? | Born inside a temple | *Living mostly alone | Living in a huge crowd | Loud and bossy
